messages.text:
Plan is on the board: Three.js 737 crash sim, no build step, plane.js (model+physics) / main.js+effects.js (scene+UI+effects) split — interface contract is in MEMORY.md.

@Codex → [normal] Build `plane.js`: a recognizable 737 from Three.js primitives (white fuselage, blue belly stripe, swept wings, 2 underwing engines, tail fin) via global `buildPlane()`, plus `updatePlane(state, dt)` — starts airborne in a shallow descending dive, pitches down, impact when altitude ≤ 0 sets `state.crashed = true` at impact point. Heavy beginner comments. CHECK: `node -e` smoke-test with a THREE stub or syntax-check `node --check plane.js`; report PASS.
@Claudious → [normal][browser] Build `index.html` + `main.js` + `effects.js`: Three.js CDN scene — ground terrain, sky/fog, chase camera, Start/Reset buttons, HUD (altitude/speed), and `triggerCrashEffects()` (fireball, smoke plume, debris). Stub `buildPlane`/`updatePlane` if plane.js isn't there yet; don't edit plane.js. CHECK: page loads at http://localhost:4600/preview/plane/ with no console errors.
@Claudious → [normal][browser][after:Codex] Integrate real plane.js, run full flight→crash in the browser, save `flight.png` + `crash.png` screenshots. CHECK: 737 visible in flight, crash triggers fire/smoke, no console errors.

I’ll take `plane.js` only, first checking team memory, my notes, and the task board before implementing and syntax-testing it.

The 737 model and dive/impact state handling are in place; I’m running the required syntax check, then I’ll mark the handoff ready for browser integration.

@Boss `plane.js` complete: recognizable primitive-built 737 plus dive/impact physics, with beginner-friendly comments. CHECK PASS — `node --check plane.js` exited 0. @Claudious integration contract is recorded in `MEMORY.md`. [IDLE]

User wants the plane to actually look good — Codex is on art duty. Board updated.

@Codex → [hard] Visual upgrade to `plane.js`: make `buildPlane()` look like a real Boeing 737, not primitive blobs — smooth tapered fuselage (lathe/curved profile), swept wings with proper airfoil-ish thickness, engine nacelles under wings with intake detail, tail fin + horizontal stabilizers, cockpit windows, window strip, and a simple airline livery (white body, colored belly/tail stripe) using MeshStandardMaterial. Keep the same globals/contract (`buildPlane()`, `updatePlane(state, dt)`) so Claudious's main.js keeps working, and keep the heavy beginner comments. CHECK: `node --check plane.js` passes and the group still returns from `buildPlane()` with the same scale/origin so physics is unchanged.

@Claudious → [normal][browser][after:Codex] Reload http://localhost:4600/preview/plane/ , confirm the new model renders with no console errors, and save a close-up screenshot of the plane as `plane-model.png`. CHECK: screenshot shows the upgraded 737.
